module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.Meromorphic.FittingIdeals
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleDescent.InvertibleInput
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSectionSequence.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.QuasicoherentBaseChange
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Module

/-!
# Stacks Tag 02OQ: the defining ideal of the zero scheme of a section

The zero scheme of a global section `t` of an invertible module `L` on a scheme `X` is
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` of the affine-local family

`J(U) = span { φ (t|_U) : φ ∈ Hom_{Γ(X,U)}(Γ(L,U), Γ(X,U)) }`,

and `ofIdeals` returns the **largest quasi-coherent** ideal sheaf *contained in* that family, so
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_ofIdeals_le` alone gives only one inclusion. This file proves the
reverse one, by showing that `J` already satisfies the single compatibility condition
`Scheme.IdealSheafData` asks of a family of ideals; `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals_ideal` then
identifies `ofIdeals J` with `J` outright.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Tag02OQSectionIdeal.map_sectionFamily_basicOpen`: the family is compatible with passage
  to a basic open.
* `Stacks.Tag02OQSectionIdeal.zeroScheme_ideal`: **Stacks Tag 02OQ's defining-ideal assertion.**
  The ideal of the zero scheme on an affine open is the whole family there.

## Why localisation of a Hom-module is the content

Compatibility is the equation `J(U)·Γ(X, D(f)) = J(D(f))`, and each inclusion is a statement
about linear functionals rather than about ideals:

* **`⊆`** needs every functional on `Γ(L, U)` to *extend* to one on `Γ(L, D(f))`. That is the
  universal property of a localisation, since `Γ(L, D(f))` is the localisation of `Γ(L, U)` at
  `f` — quasi-coherence of `L`, in the form
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ`.
* **`⊇`** needs every functional on `Γ(L, D(f))` to come from one on `Γ(L, U)` *after
  multiplication by a power of `f`*, and this is the direction that uses more than
  quasi-coherence: it is exactly surjectivity of
  `IsLocalizedModule.mapExtendScalars`, which holds because `Γ(L, U)` is a **finitely presented**
  `Γ(X, U)`-module (`Module.FinitePresentation.isLocalizedModule_mapExtendScalars`). Finite
  presentation of the sections comes from invertibility of `L` through
  `Stacks.ModuleDescent.isFinitePresentation_of_isInvertible` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.finitePresentation_sections_on_affine`.

A power of `f` becomes a unit downstairs, so dividing by it stays inside the extended ideal; that
last step is the same one as in
`Stacks.DenominatorIdealQcoh.map_rangeFamily_basicOpen`, which proves the analogous statement for
the family of *images* of a quasi-coherent submodule of the structure sheaf. That lemma does not
apply here: the family below is cut out by *all* linear functionals on the sections of `L`, not by
the sections of a fixed module mapping to `𝒪_X`, and identifying the two would need the dual sheaf
`L^∨` together with its quasi-coherence.

## Implementation notes

The family is written out rather than taken from `Stacks.RegularSectionSequence.zeroScheme`, so
that `Stacks.Tag02OQSectionIdeal.sectionIdealSheafData` can be an `IdealSheafData` whose `ideal`
field is syntactically that family; `zeroScheme_ideal` then needs only
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals_ideal`. That the written family is the one `zeroScheme` uses is
checked by elaboration in `Stacks.Tag02OQSectionIdeal.zeroScheme_eq_ofIdeals`, which is `rfl`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C6K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6K)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange

universe u

namespace Stacks.Tag02OQSectionIdeal

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The affine-local family of ideals cut out by a global section of a module: on an affine open
`U`, the ideal generated by the values of the restricted section under all `Γ(X, U)`-linear
functionals on `Γ(L, U)`. -/
def sectionFamily (L : X.Modules) (t : Γ(L, ⊤)) (U : X.affineOpens) : Ideal Γ(X, U.1) :=
  Ideal.span {a : Γ(X, U.1) | ∃ φ : Γ(L, U.1) →ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1),
    a = φ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op t)}

/-- The zero scheme of `Stacks.RegularSectionSequence.zeroScheme` is `ofIdeals` of
`Stacks.Tag02OQSectionIdeal.sectionFamily`, on the nose. -/
theorem zeroScheme_eq_ofIdeals (L : X.Modules) (t : Γ(L, ⊤)) :
    Stacks.RegularSectionSequence.zeroScheme X L t =
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals (sectionFamily L t) :=
  rfl

/-- The restriction of a global section to a basic open factors through its restriction to the
surrounding affine open. -/
theorem restrictₗ_restrict_top (L : X.Modules) (t : Γ(L, ⊤)) (U : X.affineOpens)
    (f : Γ(X, U.1)) :
    letI := moduleOfLE L (X.basicOpen_le f)
    restrictₗ L (X.basicOpen_le f) (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U.1 ≤ ⊤)).op t) =
      L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : X.basicOpen f ≤ ⊤)).op t := by
  let := moduleOfLE L (X.basicOpen_le f)
  show L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le f)).op
      (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U.1 ≤ ⊤)).op t) = _
  rw [← L.presheaf.map_comp_apply]
  congr 1

/-- **The family cut out by a global section of an invertible module is compatible with passage to
a basic open.**  This is the one condition `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData` asks of a
family of ideals; see the module documentation for why each inclusion is a statement about
localisation of linear functionals.

The target is written as a span over `X.basicOpen f` rather than as
`Stacks.Tag02OQSectionIdeal.sectionFamily L t (X.affineBasicOpen f)`: the two are the same term,
but the ring of the second is spelled `Γ(X, ↑(X.affineBasicOpen f))`, and at that spelling neither
the `Algebra Γ(X, U)`-structure nor the scalar action used below is found by instance search.
`Stacks.Tag02OQSectionIdeal.map_sectionFamily_basicOpen` is this statement at the other
spelling. -/
theorem map_sectionFamily_basicOpen' (L : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]
    (t : Γ(L, ⊤)) (U : X.affineOpens) (f : Γ(X, U.1)) :
    (sectionFamily L t U).map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le f)).op).hom =
      Ideal.span {a : Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) |
        ∃ φ : Γ(L, X.basicOpen f) →ₗ[Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)] Γ(X, X.basicOpen f),
          a = φ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op t)} := by
  have : SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation (R := X.ringCatSheaf) L :=
    Stacks.ModuleDescent.isFinitePresentation_of_isInvertible X L inferInstance
  have : L.IsQuasicoherent := SheafOfModules.instIsQuasicoherentOfIsFinitePresentation L
  have : Module.FinitePresentation Γ(X, U.1) Γ(L, U.1) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.finitePresentation_sections_on_affine L U
  let := moduleOfLE L (X.basicOpen_le f)
  have : IsLocalizedModule.Away f (restrictₗ L (X.basicOpen_le f)) :=
    isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ L U.2 f rfl (X.basicOpen_le f)
  have : IsLocalization.Away f Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) := U.2.isLocalization_basicOpen f
  have : IsScalarTower Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) Γ(L, X.basicOpen f) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun _ _ => rfl
  -- The localisation of the module of linear functionals.
  set E := IsLocalizedModule.mapExtendScalars (Submonoid.powers f)
      (restrictₗ L (X.basicOpen_le f))
      (Algebra.linearMap Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) with hEdef
  have hE : ∀ (φ : Γ(L, U.1) →ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1)) (x : Γ(L, U.1)),
      E φ (restrictₗ L (X.basicOpen_le f) x) =
        algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) (φ x) := by
    intro φ x
    rw [hEdef, IsLocalizedModule.mapExtendScalars_apply_apply, IsLocalizedModule.map_apply]
    rfl
  have key : ∀ φ : Γ(L, U.1) →ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1),
      E φ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : X.basicOpen f ≤ ⊤)).op t) =
        algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)
          (φ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U.1 ≤ ⊤)).op t)) := fun φ => by
    rw [← restrictₗ_restrict_top L t U f]
    exact hE φ _
  rw [sectionFamily]
  refine le_antisymm (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_))
    (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · -- Every functional upstairs extends to one downstairs.
    rintro a ⟨φ, rfl⟩
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨E φ, (key φ).symm⟩
  · -- Every functional downstairs is an extended one divided by a power of `f`.
    rintro a ⟨ψ, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨⟨φ, c⟩, hc⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.surj (Submonoid.powers f) E ψ
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ : IsUnit (algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) (c : Γ(X, U.1))) :=
      IsLocalization.map_units (M := Submonoid.powers f) _ c
    have hcψ : algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) (c : Γ(X, U.1)) *
        ψ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : X.basicOpen f ≤ ⊤)).op t) =
        algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)
          (φ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U.1 ≤ ⊤)).op t)) := by
      rw [← Algebra.smul_def, ← key φ, ← hc]
      exact (LinearMap.smul_apply _ _ _).symm
    have hdiv : ψ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : X.basicOpen f ≤ ⊤)).op t) =
        ((w⁻¹ : Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)ˣ) : Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)) *
          algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)
            (φ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U.1 ≤ ⊤)).op t)) := by
      rw [← hcψ, ← hw, ← mul_assoc, Units.inv_mul, one_mul]
    rw [hdiv]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _
      (Ideal.subset_span ⟨φ, rfl⟩))

/-- **The family cut out by a global section of an invertible module is compatible with passage to
a basic open**, at `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.affineBasicOpen`, which is the spelling
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData` asks for. -/
theorem map_sectionFamily_basicOpen (L : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]
    (t : Γ(L, ⊤)) (U : X.affineOpens) (f : Γ(X, U.1)) :
    (sectionFamily L t U).map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le f)).op).hom =
      sectionFamily L t (X.affineBasicOpen f) :=
  map_sectionFamily_basicOpen' L t U f

/-- The family cut out by a global section of an invertible module, as ideal-sheaf data. -/
def sectionIdealSheafData (L : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]
    (t : Γ(L, ⊤)) : X.IdealSheafData where
  ideal := sectionFamily L t
  map_ideal_basicOpen := map_sectionFamily_basicOpen L t

/-- **Stacks Tag 02OQ, the defining ideal of the zero scheme.**  On every affine open the ideal of
the zero scheme of a global section of an invertible module is the ideal generated by the values of
the restricted section under all linear functionals there.

`Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` is a supremum and in general shrinks the family it is applied to;
it does not here, because that family is already compatible with passage to a basic open and hence
is itself an ideal sheaf. -/
@[stacks 02OQ "the defining ideal"]
theorem zeroScheme_ideal (L : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]
    (t : Γ(L, ⊤)) (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (Stacks.RegularSectionSequence.zeroScheme X L t).ideal U =
      Ideal.span {a : Γ(X, U.1) | ∃ φ : Γ(L, U.1) →ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1),
        a = φ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op t)} := by
  rw [zeroScheme_eq_ofIdeals,
    show Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals (sectionFamily L t) = sectionIdealSheafData L t from
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals_ideal (sectionIdealSheafData L t)]
  rfl

end Stacks.Tag02OQSectionIdeal

end
